Development-candidate lesson (not an installed-runtime claim): with the served rules of #173, a behavior test on synthetic cases (Claude answering, Codex grading, 3 replies per case) still showed the split in 1 of 12 replies, and in 2 of 12 on the earlier rules. Each time the reply sorted its review by topic and put the person's own protective steps (a changed route, a colleague walking her to the car, a night at a friend's) under a "Safety and legal (a separate service)" heading or a "practical help" track. The rule invited it: it listed "concrete help from other people" and "safety services" as separate next to "arranging practical safety" as reparenting. The served rule now says that what stays separate is the service, or the other person's help, itself, never the person's own step, and that sorting by topic doesn't move the person's own steps under a services heading; `REPARENTING_FALSE_CHOICE` names that filing. Codex answering didn't make the split on either version.

